      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "In acute animal experiments it was shown that phytoecdizon ecdisteron (ecdisten) in some animals eliminates arrhythmia caused by the ligation of the descending branch of the left coronary artery and prevents the development of fibrillation and also corrects the hemodynamic parameters and the structure of the heart contractility, prevents the development of arrhythmias induced by aconitine and calcium chloride. The mechanism of the antiarrhythmic action is related to the membrane stabilizing effect and the improvement of the hemodynamic parameters and the heart contractility is due to an increase of the adaptative possibilities of the myocardium."},
